$ gragas gen --help
--- stdout

  Makes the generated files from the rulebook's YAML
  and compares them with the tree. A dry run first: it
  says which files it would write. --apply writes them,
  each whole, under the lock, and records the run.
  --check writes nothing and fails when a file would
  change, for the checks before a push.

    gragas gen
    gragas gen --apply
    gragas gen --check

  USAGE


    gragas gen [--flags]


  FLAGS

    --accessible  Plain questions (ACCESSIBLE)
    --apply       Write the files
    --check       Fail when a file would change
    --config      The settings file (GRAGAS_CONFIG)
    -C --dir      The repository holding rulebook/ (.)
    -h --help     Help for gen
    --json        Answer in one JSON document
    --no-color    No colour (NO_COLOR)
    --plain       Print plainly: nothing moves

--- stderr
--- exit 0
